        "original_target": "If a lift u has a typed recovery of old terms on the old image, then u is injective. Off-image rejection, observation preservation and obstruction repair do not follow (WDP-P001-006: off_image_not_implied, observation_not_implied, repair_not_implied).",
        "source_scope_review": "No operation candidate was recovered, so the declarations were mined by hand: Paper.lean line 54 (old_image_injective, a general theorem over arbitrary types A B E) and Paper001.lean lines 103 (E = Unit), 111, 128, 138. The injectivity theorem is general and non-vacuous. The three negative-boundary theorems are fixed Fin instances (off_image_not_implied: u constant 0 and r constant inl 0 on Fin 1 -> Fin 2; observation_not_implied: identity on Fin 2; repair_not_implied: the constant-true predicate on Fin 1), and repair_not_implied states only that a constant-true predicate stays true, so it defines no repair. This node proves the general forms of the first two boundaries, a converse and an exact count, keeps the repair statement at the weak persistence reading, and enumerates all (u, r) pairs for small finite sets to see that the claim could fail on them.",
        "admitted_assumptions": []
      },
